      "answer": "Tension $=2.05\\,\\mathrm{N}$ and $\\alpha=76.9^\\circ$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Attempt to resolve either direction [M1: correct number of terms; allow sine/cosine mix, sign errors and missing $g$].\n\n$0.3g+T\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-4\\sin60^\\circ=0$ ($T\\cos\\alpha^\\circ=0.464\\ldots$) [A1 OE].\n\n$T\\sin\\alpha^\\circ-4\\cos60^\\circ=0$ ($T\\sin\\alpha^\\circ=2$) [A1 OE; if the two $T$s differ, maximum A1A0 unless subsequently stated equal].\n\n$\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{4\\cos60^\\circ}{4\\sin60^\\circ-0.3g}\\right)=\\tan^{-1}(2/0.464\\ldots)$ [M1: attempt to solve for $\\alpha$, no missing/extra terms; allow missing $g$; must reach $\\alpha=$].\n\n$T=\\frac{4\\cos60^\\circ}{\\sin(\\text{their }\\alpha)}=\\sqrt{(4\\cos60^\\circ)^2+(4\\sin60^\\circ-0.3g)^2}$ [M1 OE: attempt to solve for $T$, no missing/extra terms; allow missing $g$; must reach $T=$].\n\nTension $=2.05\\,\\mathrm{N}$, $\\alpha=76.9^\\circ$ [A1 for both; AWRT $2.05,76.9$; exact calculator values $2.05314\\ldots,76.9356\\ldots$].\n\nAlternative, triangle of forces: attempt cosine rule using lengths $4$ and $0.3g$ with a suitable angle [M1; allow missing $g$]; $T^2=4^2+(0.3g)^2-2(4)(0.3g)\\cos30^\\circ$ [A1]; $T=2.05$ [A1, AWRT]. Attempt sine rule [M1: angle $30^\\circ$ and another angle in terms of $\\alpha$, correct numerators; allow missing $g$]; $\\frac{\\text{their }T}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac4{\\sin(180^\\circ-\\alpha)}$ or $\\frac{\\text{their }T}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{0.3g}{\\sin(\\alpha-30^\\circ)}$ [A1; allow $\\sin\\alpha$ instead of $\\sin(180^\\circ-\\alpha)$]; $\\alpha=76.9^\\circ$ [A1, AWRT].\n\nAlternative, Lami's theorem: attempt Lami [M1; numerators correct and at least one angle correct; allow missing $g$]; $\\frac4{\\sin\\alpha}=\\frac{0.3g}{\\sin(210^\\circ-\\alpha)}=\\frac{T}{\\sin150^\\circ}$ [A1 A1: first A1 for two parts, second for all three]; $\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{4\\sin210^\\circ}{0.3g+4\\cos210^\\circ}\\right)$ [M1: compound-angle solution, correct for their angles; allow missing $g$]; $T=\\frac{4\\sin150^\\circ}{\\sin\\alpha}$ or $T=\\frac{0.3g\\sin150^\\circ}{\\sin(210^\\circ-\\alpha)}$ [M1; their $\\alpha$; allow missing $g$]; tension $=2.05\\,\\mathrm{N}$, $\\alpha=76.9^\\circ$ [A1 for both, AWRT].\n\nSC: tension and the $4\\,\\mathrm{N}$ force considered in the wrong directions. Attempt to resolve either direction [M1; correct terms; allow sine/cosine mix, sign errors and missing $g$]; $T\\cos60^\\circ-4\\sin\\alpha^\\circ=0$ and $T\\sin60^\\circ-4\\cos\\alpha^\\circ-0.3g=0$ [A1 for both OE; if two $T$s differ, SC A0 unless later equated]; attempt to solve for $T$ or $\\alpha$ [M1 OE; no missing/extra terms; allow missing $g$; must reach $T=$ or $\\alpha=$], e.g. $(T\\cos60^\\circ/4)^2+((T\\sin60^\\circ-0.3g)/4)^2=1\\Rightarrow T^2-3\\sqrt3T-7=0\\Rightarrow T=6.31$ (or $-1.11$), or $4\\sqrt3\\sin\\alpha-4\\cos\\alpha=3\\Rightarrow8\\sin(\\alpha-30^\\circ)=3\\Rightarrow\\alpha=\\sin^{-1}(3/8)+30^\\circ$; $T=6.31\\,\\mathrm{N}$, $\\alpha=52.0^\\circ$ [A1; exact values $6.30617\\ldots,52.0243\\ldots$]. Total: 6.",
